<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.088 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.088 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$3.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due June 19 was 3.088 percent, up from 2.993 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.5 billion of 175-day T-bills due September 11, 1997 was 3.418 percent, up from 3.285 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due March 19, 1998 was 3.900 percent, up from 3.743 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$550 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.0 billion of C$5.4 billion bills due March 27.</p>
